.TH wmapplications 1 "2026" "Window Maker"
.SH NAME
wmapplications \- choose default desktop applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmapplications
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmapplications
is a WINGs dialog for selecting a web browser, email client, terminal
emulator, file manager and archive manager from installed desktop entries.
It requires a build with GIO desktop application support.
.PP
The Apply button saves changed selections using GIO and the freedesktop.org
MIME Applications specification. Only MIME types and URL schemes declared
by the chosen application are changed. Other associations are preserved.
The browser covers HTTP, HTTPS and HTML, email covers mailto, and the file
manager covers directories. The archive manager covers common ZIP, tar,
gzip, bzip2, XZ, 7z, RAR and Zstandard formats that it supports.
.PP
If existing associations differ or no default is configured, the dialog
shows "Keep existing defaults". This option never changes associations.
Saving multiple associations is not transactional: an error is reported
if saving fails, but earlier successful changes may remain.
.PP
Terminal selection uses the proposed xdg-terminal-exec configuration,
not a MIME association. It is enabled only when xdg-terminal-exec is
installed and compatible terminal desktop entries are available.
Eligible entries have the TerminalEmulator category and an
X-TerminalArgExec or TerminalArgExec key, which may be empty.
The selected desktop ID is prepended to the highest-priority applicable
user xdg-terminals.list file. Existing comments, directives and fallback
preferences are retained.
This setting affects programs using xdg-terminal-exec, not legacy terminal
commands, shell environment variables or system alternatives.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " host:display.screen"
specify display to use.
.TP
.BR \-\-help " | " \-h
print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version " | " \-v
print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mimeapps.list
User MIME application associations managed by GIO.
Desktop-specific associations may take precedence.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xdg-terminals.list
User terminal preferences. A desktop-specific file named
desktop-xdg-terminals.list is used when XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP is set.
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config.
Applications are discovered in the XDG data hierarchy's applications
directories, including ~/.local/share/applications and /usr/share/applications.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR WPrefs (1),
.BR xdg-mime (1),
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1)
